  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes across both lotteries, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the decision problem are: -4000, 0 (from Lottery A), and -3000, 0 (from Lottery B). Ignoring probabilities, the set of outcomes is [-4000, 0, -3000, 0]. The mean (aspiration level) is (-4000 + 0 + (-3000) + 0) / 4 = -1750. Next, the reason evaluates each lottery by computing the difference between each outcome and the aspiration level (-1750), and checks the probability that an outcome exceeds this level (i.e., has a positive difference). For Lottery A: -4000 - (-1750) = -2250 (negative), 0 - (-1750) = +1750 (positive). So, positive difference occurs with 80% probability. For Lottery B: -3000 - (-1750) = -1250 (negative), 0 - (-1750) = +1750 (positive). Positive difference occurs with 75% probability. Since Lottery A has a higher probability (80% > 75%) of yielding a positive difference from the aspiration level, the reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the reason is applicable and leads to a preference for A.",
